  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Asj vs The State (Da) on 17 October, 2016 1 In The Court Of Sh. Rakesh Pandit, Asj-01, New Delhi District, Patiala House Courts, New Delhi Ca No. 8640/16 1 Inderdeo Tripathi S/o Sh. G. N. Tripathi, R/o C-123, Naraina, Industrial Area, Phase-1, New Delhi-110028. 2 M/s Som Products, Through Shri Inderdeo Tripathi ....Appellants Vs. The State (Da) .... Respondent Date of receiving of Appeal : 24.02.2016 Date of arguments : 17.10.2016 Date of judgment : 17.10.2016 Judgment",
    "facts": "The brief facts of the case as per record and from trial court record are that accused is running an establishment namely M/s Som Products at C-123, Naraina Industrial Area, New Delhi- 110028. On 08.04.2008 at about 11.45 a.m. Food Inspector Sh. Prem Chand Tiwari visited the said place and purchased 9 sealed poly packets of \"Flavoured Pan Masala\" each containing 60 pouches of two grams (ready for sale) from accused/appellant. FI was accompanied with SDM/LHA Sh. S. M. Bhardwaj. The said Pan Masala was purchased for the purposes of analysis under PFA Act. The same sample was divided into three parts, packed as per Rules of PFA. One sample was sent for analysis to Public Analyst. As per the report of Analyst, sample did not confirm to the standard because \"The sample is misbranded because there is violation of Rule-32(i). 3 As the sample was failed, prosecution was launched by Food Inspector by filing complaint dated 02.09.2008 with the court. The appellant no. 2/company i.e. M/s Som Products was directed to pay fine of Rs.50,000/-. 6 In this appeal, the accused has assailed the judgment on the following grounds:- (i) There is no requirement of writing \"best before\" on the outer package. ( ii) The outer package was not required to be sold directly to the consumer. 7 No reply was filed by respondent/state and the matter was argued orally.",
    "arguments": "9 It is argued by counsel for appellant that there is no requirement of writing \"best before\" on the outer package. It is further argued that there is no requirement for writing the same on the outer package as the outer package is not to be sold to the consumer directly.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "9 It is argued by counsel for appellant that there is no requirement of writing \"best before\" on the outer package. It is further argued that there is no requirement for writing the same on the outer package as the outer package is not to be sold to the consumer directly.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
